# 9. AI Agents, Multi-Agent Workflows, RAG & Prompt Library

## 9.1 Agent roles

- **Planner:** decomposes approved objectives
- **Retriever:** obtains tenant-authorized evidence
- **Executor:** calls permitted tools
- **Critic:** validates evidence, schema and policy
- **Safety agent:** checks sensitive data and prohibited actions
- **Cost controller:** enforces token and financial budgets
- **Human coordinator:** opens and resumes approval tasks

Agents do not receive unrestricted credentials. They call the Tool Gateway using short-lived, execution-scoped capability tokens.

## 9.2 Workflow

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> ValidateInput
    ValidateInput --> RetrieveContext
    RetrieveContext --> Plan
    Plan --> PolicyCheck
    PolicyCheck --> Execute: permitted
    PolicyCheck --> HumanApproval: elevated risk
    PolicyCheck --> Rejected: prohibited
    HumanApproval --> Execute: approved
    HumanApproval --> Rejected: denied/expired
    Execute --> ValidateOutput
    ValidateOutput --> RetryOrFallback: invalid/transient
    RetryOrFallback --> Execute
    ValidateOutput --> HumanReview: low confidence
    ValidateOutput --> Complete: valid
    HumanReview --> Complete: approved
    HumanReview --> Rejected: rejected
    Complete --> [*]
    Rejected --> [*]
```

## 9.3 Tool permission model

Plugin manifest:

